{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Re-review verdict (job …15dacd7e, reviewed_at 1793502297895881661): BLOCK, 5 findings — but only ONE is blocking (G6, decision_margin 0.0889 against a 0.80 threshold). The other four are advisory: P4 (45 file-impact entries > 30), P6 (compound AC lines; a `cat` verify command that asserts nothing), G7 (AC5 `--update-stale` vs the parent epic's Ratchet note), E1 (the `--check exits 0` clause appears in both AC2 and AC5).\n\nG6 CHECKED AGAINST THE COMMIT, NOT THE PLAN. The finding says the invariant \"No test body changes\" contradicts \"rename differing definitions and repoint their callers\" for helpers and fixtures called from inside test bodies. The finding is CORRECT about the plan's wording, and it is ALREADY SATISFIED by the committed implementation at 693030cb9ab. Both modules the reviewer cites are merged, and both renames are present with the distinctions it demanded:\n\ntests/unit/workflow/test_gate_error_sidecar.py\n  :108 `_gate_errors` — base, called at :141, :168, :206\n  :248 `_gate_errors_heldout` — held-out, called at :275, :317, :341\n\ntests/unit/reconciler/diffing/test_canonical_outbound_equivalence.py\n  :99-100 `backend` — FUNCTION-scoped, monkeypatch-sets REBAR_RECONCILER_RICH_TEXT_CUTOVER=off;\n          consumed by the 6 base tests at :109,:113,:117,:123,:206,:217\n  :299-300 `backend_heldout` — MODULE-scoped, no env pin;\n          consumed by the 3 held-out tests at :306,:316,:325\n\nThe reviewer's fourth evidence line — \"the two cannot be deduped and the rename must preserve the held-out fixture's distinct scope/body\" — is exactly what the commit does. Scope, body, and env pin all preserved; no base test's assertions, logic, or data were touched.\n\nSo the ambiguity is in the plan's prose, not in the work. The implementation chose the reading the reviewer prescribes. Recording this rather than re-running a 15-20 minute gate to reword an invariant on work that is already complete and committed.\n\nPlan-review attestation is `stale-material` (description 7797→7967, file_impact 44→45). That is the CLAIM gate; this ticket was claimed long ago. The close runs the completion-verifier gate, which is separate."},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1793503447206733996,"uuid":"e36a9f23-ab64-435c-b58a-b56c8241587b"}